      "message": "test(app): main's 3+2 first-traverse tests read the user's frame\n\nMain added two tests after the review of this PR that pin the\nFirstTraverseLow heights in the local frame of the 3+2 plane:\nfirst_traverse_table.rs (the head-tilt table verdict) and\nfirst_traverse_mill_turn.rs (the B 10 mill-turn plane). This PR gives\nthose heights in the frame where the user sets them (#2991), so the\ntests now expect the clearance as set and the top plus the origin Z.\nThe table test reads the tilted text (\"raise the clearance height by\nat least ... mm\", \"measured along the tilted tool axis\"). The post\nstays blocked in both tests.\n\nMove in_user_frame above the test module (clippy\nitems_after_test_module, after main added the module).\n\nRefs #2991\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
